(MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT MSA-SRS-2026-014) Tj T*
(This Agreement is between Merrow County Emergency Management Agency \(Owner\) and Southeastern) Tj T*
(Recovery Services, LLC \(Contractor\) for debris removal after Tropical Storm Alder. Effective) Tj T*
(date: March 1, 2026.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Scope) Tj T*
(Contractor shall collect, haul, reduce, and dispose of eligible storm debris within Merrow) Tj T*
(County at the Owner's direction, under task orders issued by the Owner's Debris Manager.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Order of Precedence) Tj T*
(If contract documents conflict, the later executed written amendment controls for work) Tj T*
(performed on or after its effective date, then Pricing Schedule PS-A-2026-014, then this) Tj T*
(Agreement. Contractor procedures, including SRS-OPS-SOP-07, are not contract documents and) Tj T*
(never control over them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Term) Tj T*
(The initial term runs through February 28, 2027, unless ended earlier under Section 11.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Task Orders) Tj T*
(No work is payable without a written task order naming the debris type, the work zone, and) Tj T*
(the approved disposal site.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Measurement and Payment) Tj T*
(5.1 Payment is by unit rate in the Pricing Schedule in effect on the date of service.) Tj T*
(5.2 Every load requires a load ticket showing ticket number, date, truck, debris type, load) Tj T*
(call percentage, one-way miles, disposal site, and monitor initials. A ticket without) Tj T*
(monitor initials is not payable until corrected by the monitor.) Tj T*
(5.3 Payable volume equals the truck's certified capacity multiplied by the monitor's load) Tj T*
(call percentage.) Tj T*
(5.4 Payable volume is rounded down to the nearest whole cubic yard for each ticket.) Tj T*
(5.5 A load call under 50 percent is not payable unless the Contractor's Project Director) Tj T*
(reviews it and the Owner concurs in writing.) Tj T*
(5.6 A load containing both vegetative and construction and demolition debris shall be) Tj T*
(classified by the Contractor's Project Director before billing. That classification may not) Tj T*
(be delegated or automated.) Tj T*
(5.7 A physical ticket may be billed only once, however many times it is recorded.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Mileage) Tj T*
(Mileage bands use one-way haul miles along the shortest legal truck route from the load site) Tj T*
(to the disposal site.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Truck Certification) Tj T*
(Each truck must appear on the Truck Certification Register \(SRS-TCR-2026\) with a measured) Tj T*
(capacity before hauling. A ticket for a truck not on the register is not payable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Invoicing) Tj T*
(Contractor shall invoice monthly, with a ticket-level backup workbook, within 30 calendar) Tj T*
(days after month end. Late invoices may be rejected at the Owner's discretion. The) Tj T*
(Contractor's Project Director must approve each invoice before submission.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
