(9. Retainage) Tj T*
(The Owner may hold five percent retainage on each invoice until final acceptance of the work) Tj T*
(zone.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(10. Records and Audit) Tj T*
(Contractor shall keep all tickets, certifications, and invoices for seven years and produce) Tj T*
(them on request. Ticket corrections must preserve the original entry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(11. Termination) Tj T*
(The Owner may terminate for convenience on 15 days written notice, and shall pay for work) Tj T*
(properly performed through the termination date.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(12. Insurance) Tj T*
(Contractor shall maintain commercial general liability of not less than two million dollars) Tj T*
(per occurrence, with the Owner named as additional insured, plus statutory workers) Tj T*
(compensation coverage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(13. Environmental Compliance) Tj T*
(Contractor shall haul only to approved disposal sites, keep hazardous material out of debris) Tj T*
(loads, and report any release within 24 hours. Debris may not be stockpiled outside an) Tj T*
(approved temporary debris storage and reduction site.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(14. Safety) Tj T*
(Contractor shall maintain a written safety plan, flag crews for work in public rights of) Tj T*
(way, and report recordable incidents to the Debris Manager within one business day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(15. Subcontractors) Tj T*
(Subcontractors require the Owner's written consent. Contractor remains responsible for) Tj T*
(subcontractor tickets, certifications, and invoicing accuracy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(16. Disputes) Tj T*
(The parties shall first attempt to resolve disputes between the Debris Manager and the) Tj T*
(Project Director. An unresolved dispute goes to the Owner's Director within ten business) Tj T*
(days, then to non-binding mediation before any action at law.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(17. Notices) Tj T*
(Notices must be written and delivered to the addresses on the signature page. Email counts) Tj T*
(only when the recipient acknowledges receipt in writing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(18. Entire Agreement) Tj T*
(This Agreement, its Pricing Schedule, and any written amendment signed by both parties are) Tj T*
(the entire agreement. No course of dealing changes these terms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(19. Severability) Tj T*
(If a court finds a provision unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay in force, and the) Tj T*
(parties shall replace that provision with one that most nearly reflects the original intent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
